  "id": "hemispheric-asymmetry-reduction-in-older-adults",
  "term": "hemispheric asymmetry reduction in older adults",
  "definition": "Hemispheric asymmetry reduction in older adults (HAROLD) is an age-related pattern in which brain activity becomes less strongly concentrated in one hemisphere during cognitive tasks. In the packet, it is described as a neurocompensatory process, meaning this reduced lateralization may help support performance in older adults.",
